# __NAME__

A native app on [Rune](https://github.com/anomalyco/rune): Rust, rendered with
`wgpu` and `winit`, with the framework's own layout and text shaping. A Rune app
is a plain crate — `Cargo.toml` and `src/main.rs`, nothing generated.

## Commands

- Build: `cargo build`
- Run: `cargo run`
- Test: `cargo test`
- Headless snapshot: `cargo run -- --scene default --snap out.png --tree tree.json`
- Typecheck: `cargo check` (typechecker `__TYPECHECKER__`)
- Lint: `cargo clippy -- -D warnings` (linter `__LINTER__`)
- Format: `cargo fmt` (formatter `__FORMATTER__`)

## Notes

- The framework is pinned by `rev` in `Cargo.toml`. Keep it pinned: `dev` moves.
- `AppSpec` is built as a literal ending `..AppSpec::new(..)` so a new upstream
  field does not break this file.
- `scenes` in `AppSpec` is what lets `--snap` render a non-default state.
- Prerequisites: Rust >= 1.85 (edition 2024); on Linux also `libxkbcommon-dev`
  and `libwayland-dev`, plus `mesa-vulkan-drivers` for software rendering.
- Rune has no HTTP client. A network call is your own dependency.
